WEBVTT

00:34.617 --> 00:36.661
Is that a sword?

00:36.745 --> 00:40.957
It has to be
at least 300 years old, right?

00:41.708 --> 00:42.792
You're right.

00:42.876 --> 00:45.962
Isn't this bad? What should we do?

00:48.339 --> 00:51.134
-I can't contain my excitement!
-Me neither!

00:51.718 --> 00:55.138
Tanjiro, you didn't get
your newly forged sword, right?

00:55.722 --> 00:58.391
Maybe you should take it?

00:58.475 --> 01:01.061
No, no, no! I can't take it!

01:01.144 --> 01:04.564
Steel from the Sengoku period
is high quality!

01:04.647 --> 01:06.316
Don't talk me into taking it!

01:06.399 --> 01:09.194
We found it because you shattered it.

01:09.277 --> 01:12.155
Just because it had been damaged
many times already.

01:12.238 --> 01:15.450
It just happened to break
while I was training with it.

01:15.533 --> 01:17.702
Are you sure you won't take it?

01:20.038 --> 01:22.540
Want to try pulling it out?

01:22.624 --> 01:24.959
Yeah, I want to see the sword!

01:31.049 --> 01:32.342
It's rusty.

01:33.343 --> 01:35.762
Well, it's only natural.

01:35.845 --> 01:37.222
Given no one knew about it,

01:37.305 --> 01:39.891
no one took care of it
for three centuries.

01:39.974 --> 01:42.644
Sorry to dash your hopes.

01:43.311 --> 01:46.064
It's okay. I don't mind.

01:47.273 --> 01:48.233
Tanjiro!

01:48.316 --> 01:50.652
Tanjiro, I'm really sorry!

01:52.695 --> 01:54.030
What's that?

02:17.512 --> 02:20.515
Demon Slayer: Swordsmith Village Arc

03:34.172 --> 03:38.927
Episode 3:
A Sword from Over 300 Years Ago

03:44.224 --> 03:46.517
Wait, who is it? Is that you, Haganezuka?

03:47.018 --> 03:49.520
I heard everything.

03:49.604 --> 03:51.689
Leave it to me.

03:51.773 --> 03:53.399
Leave what to you?

03:55.735 --> 03:57.528
What are you doing?

03:57.612 --> 03:59.656
Leave it to me.

03:59.739 --> 04:03.534
Please, let go of it!
Why are you trying to take it away?

04:03.618 --> 04:06.037
Shut up and leave it to me!

04:06.120 --> 04:10.458
Why do you show up out of the blue
and tell us to leave it to you?

04:10.541 --> 04:12.043
Just leave it to me!

04:12.126 --> 04:14.545
No! This is Kotetsu's!

04:14.629 --> 04:16.172
Leave it to me!

04:16.256 --> 04:20.551
I came here to see you.
Where have you been?

04:24.138 --> 04:26.307
If I say leave it to me,
just leave it to me!

04:26.391 --> 04:31.437
Leave what to you? Explain yourself!

04:31.521 --> 04:33.898
I said leave it to me!

04:35.650 --> 04:38.444
An adult shouldn't act like that!

04:39.237 --> 04:43.241
Boys, Haganezuka's weak spot is his sides.

04:43.324 --> 04:45.034
Right here.

04:45.118 --> 04:48.288
Tickle, tickle.

04:48.371 --> 04:51.624
Kanamori. Long time no see.

04:51.708 --> 04:54.419
Hello, Tanjiro.

04:54.502 --> 04:58.047
Haganezuka will be exhausted for a while
after being tickled.

04:58.131 --> 05:00.008
So let me explain it to you.

05:01.384 --> 05:04.137
Please, forgive Haganezuka.

05:04.762 --> 05:08.016
Well, he was secluding himself
in the mountains for training.

05:08.099 --> 05:09.517
Training?

05:09.600 --> 05:14.897
Yes. In order to be able to make
a stronger sword so you won't die.

05:16.649 --> 05:19.152
He won't be honest about it, though.

05:19.777 --> 05:21.362
For me?

05:22.780 --> 05:26.534
You've entrusted him
to make you a sword, right?

05:26.617 --> 05:28.911
I think he was happy about that.

05:28.995 --> 05:33.499
He was often out of charge
because the swordsmen detest him.

05:33.583 --> 05:34.917
Is that so?

05:35.668 --> 05:38.379
He sucks at socializing, you know.

05:38.463 --> 05:41.257
That's why he hasn't gotten married yet.

05:42.091 --> 05:44.343
He's back.

05:45.094 --> 05:48.389
I will take this rusty sword

05:48.473 --> 05:54.937
and polish it using the Nichirin Sword
polishing art of the Haganezuka family.

05:55.021 --> 05:58.357
Then why not just say so from the start?

05:58.441 --> 06:01.569
All you said was, "Leave it to me!"
even though we don't know other.

06:01.652 --> 06:03.905
Like an idiot
who can only remember one thing.

06:03.988 --> 06:08.284
What did you say? Say it again!

06:08.367 --> 06:09.952
You're choking me…

06:10.036 --> 06:13.498
His sides! His sides! Aim at his sides!

06:24.592 --> 06:29.013
While I'm taking care of this one,
use this sword instead.

06:36.479 --> 06:38.231
Thank you.

06:39.315 --> 06:41.567
That's what happened yesterday.

06:41.651 --> 06:45.113
Apparently, it'll take three days
and three nights to polish that sword.

06:45.696 --> 06:47.949
So he'll finish it the day after tomorrow.

06:48.032 --> 06:50.743
I'm worried
because it said the polishing method

06:50.827 --> 06:53.621
is so harsh that people have gotten killed
as a result.

06:54.288 --> 06:57.500
But he forbade me from peeking.

06:57.583 --> 06:59.127
Do you think I can take a look?

06:59.210 --> 07:01.254
I don't give a shit! Get out!

07:01.337 --> 07:03.798
Don't talk to me like I'm your friend!

07:03.881 --> 07:06.342
Huh? We aren't friends?

07:06.425 --> 07:08.261
Of course not!

07:08.344 --> 07:10.763
You broke my arm, remember?

07:10.847 --> 07:12.765
Don't tell me you forgot.

07:15.768 --> 07:18.938
Genya, it was your own fault
for hitting that girl.

07:19.021 --> 07:20.022
I had to.

07:20.106 --> 07:22.233
Don't call me by my first name!

07:22.859 --> 07:25.403
These rice crackers are delicious.
Do you want one?

07:25.486 --> 07:26.487
No, shit!

07:26.571 --> 07:29.073
I don't want it! Get lost!

07:29.907 --> 07:35.705
Wasn't your front tooth missing
at the hot spring?

07:43.129 --> 07:45.214
You must be mistaken.

07:45.298 --> 07:48.468
I know I'm not mistaken.
I still have it, here.

07:48.801 --> 07:52.472
Why did you keep it?
You're freaking disgusting!

07:52.555 --> 07:55.516
Well, you dropped it,
so I wanted to return it.

07:55.600 --> 07:58.478
Are you out of your mind? Throw it away!

07:58.561 --> 07:59.896
Get the hell out!

08:09.947 --> 08:13.409
Like this, this, and then like this.

08:14.035 --> 08:17.163
Next, this way.

08:17.955 --> 08:21.042
Why is Genya always so angry?

08:21.125 --> 08:24.045
I wonder if he's still hungry.

08:24.879 --> 08:28.424
I think I'll invite Genya
to have a meal tomorrow morning.

08:31.010 --> 08:32.929
You think it's a good idea, Nezuko?

08:33.012 --> 08:37.016
We've had a bath together,
so we should have a meal together next.

08:38.726 --> 08:41.771
I'd like to get to know Genya better.

08:43.773 --> 08:46.317
Braiding is difficult.

08:46.400 --> 08:49.987
Now you have the same hairstyle
as Kanroji.

08:55.284 --> 08:58.996
Nezuko, the moon looks beautiful tonight.

09:17.139 --> 09:20.017
I was in the bath for too long.

09:20.101 --> 09:22.979
I have to work early in the morning.

09:27.817 --> 09:29.068
A vase?

09:29.151 --> 09:32.613
I didn't see this when I was going up.

09:33.656 --> 09:38.244
Who put a vase out here?
It could be dangerous, you know.

10:07.231 --> 10:09.275
What a horrible flavor!

10:09.734 --> 10:15.072
The flesh of mountain swordsmiths
is simply not good for eating.

10:15.698 --> 10:18.492
But that's all right.

10:19.368 --> 10:22.413
Still, destroying this place

10:22.496 --> 10:27.376
will certainly weaken the demon hunters.

10:28.502 --> 10:32.381
Must hurry. Must hurry.

10:32.965 --> 10:36.677
Thanks to Gyokko, we found the village.

10:38.763 --> 10:42.391
But our lord is furious.

10:42.475 --> 10:44.935
Hurry. Hurry.

10:45.019 --> 10:47.355
We must kill everyone…

10:48.022 --> 10:51.484
Everyone who opposes our lord.

11:15.966 --> 11:17.843
Old man, have you finished it?

11:19.303 --> 11:20.638
No one's here.

11:32.858 --> 11:34.276
Big bro…

11:36.529 --> 11:39.156
I have to do it.

11:45.955 --> 11:48.791
Do you know a swordsmith named Kanamori?

11:48.874 --> 11:51.585
Tokito! What are you doing here?

11:51.669 --> 11:54.296
Wait, did you just pinch my nose?

11:55.005 --> 11:55.965
Yes, I did.

11:56.048 --> 11:58.175
Your reaction was too slow.

11:58.259 --> 12:02.054
Come on, I would be able to tell
if you were a bad guy.

12:02.138 --> 12:05.808
Fair enough. If I was a bad guy,
I wouldn't pinch your nose.

12:06.475 --> 12:09.520
Yeah, I know Kanamori. But why?

12:09.603 --> 12:12.815
Perhaps he's with Haganezuka.

12:13.441 --> 12:16.777
Kanamori is my new swordsmith.

12:16.861 --> 12:19.071
Where is Haganezuka?

12:19.155 --> 12:21.157
Shall we look for him together?

12:23.492 --> 12:26.454
Why do you care about people so much?

12:26.537 --> 12:29.832
Don't you have other concerns?

12:30.916 --> 12:36.380
Because helping others eventually
ends up being good for me.

12:36.464 --> 12:39.467
I was thinking of going too.
You came at the right time.

12:43.262 --> 12:45.723
What? What did you just say?

12:45.806 --> 12:47.433
Your words earlier…

12:47.516 --> 12:50.186
Huh? I said you came at the right time.

12:50.269 --> 12:51.270
Ow!

12:51.896 --> 12:54.440
Nezuko, you're awake.

12:54.523 --> 12:56.025
It hurts…

13:05.367 --> 13:07.620
Let's go to Haganezuka's together.

13:10.998 --> 13:14.793
That girl is a strange creature.

13:14.877 --> 13:16.837
Huh? Is she strange?

13:16.921 --> 13:19.173
Yeah. She's very strange.

13:19.924 --> 13:23.010
How can I say it?
I can't put it into words.

13:23.093 --> 13:26.013
Have I met her before?

13:26.096 --> 13:28.432
Was she already like this?

13:28.516 --> 13:30.184
I wonder…

13:43.030 --> 13:44.990
Is someone here?

13:45.074 --> 13:46.534
Yes, someone's here.

14:04.885 --> 14:08.681
Wait, what? Is it a demon?

14:09.515 --> 14:11.684
How did this demon get here?

14:12.351 --> 14:14.853
I didn't notice it until now.

14:15.437 --> 14:18.357
This demon is definitely an Upper Rank!

14:22.027 --> 14:23.571
Mist Breathing,

14:24.947 --> 14:27.950
Fourth Form: Shifting Flow Slash.

14:32.079 --> 14:35.249
It's fast. I didn't kill it.

14:35.332 --> 14:41.130
Please, stop. Don't attack me.

14:41.213 --> 14:43.674
It hurts!

14:43.757 --> 14:47.261
Don't hesitate!
It's a demon that's killed many people.

14:47.344 --> 14:50.472
Otherwise, it wouldn't be able
to dodge a Hashira's attack.

14:51.265 --> 14:52.766
Hinokami Kagura:

14:55.728 --> 14:57.229
Sunflower Thrust!

15:01.275 --> 15:02.735
Did I get it?

15:02.818 --> 15:06.405
Why doesn't it counterattack?
Isn't it an Upper Rank?

15:14.038 --> 15:16.457
Nezuko, don't use that form!

15:16.540 --> 15:18.751
Turn back or it will trigger
your demonification!

15:25.132 --> 15:27.509
You cut me!

15:28.052 --> 15:29.845
He severed its head.

15:29.929 --> 15:31.639
That was fast, but…

15:31.722 --> 15:35.768
Beheading Upper Ranks
doesn't mean killing them.

15:37.853 --> 15:39.939
Tokito, stay alert!

15:55.579 --> 15:57.039
He split in two!

15:57.122 --> 16:01.502
One grew a head and the other grew a body.

16:01.585 --> 16:03.337
I'll get the one in the back!

16:03.420 --> 16:05.422
As long as we cut at the same time…

16:14.348 --> 16:15.849
Nezuko!

16:16.350 --> 16:17.601
Tokito!

16:27.695 --> 16:29.863
It's really fun!

16:29.947 --> 16:32.866
That little bean went flying so far.

16:32.950 --> 16:34.994
Didn't it, Sekido?

16:35.077 --> 16:37.204
There's nothing fun about it.

16:37.287 --> 16:40.082
I'm just so angry.

16:40.165 --> 16:44.086
I'm also angry about being
mixed in with you, Karaku.

16:44.169 --> 16:45.004
PLEASURE

16:45.087 --> 16:49.216
Is that so?
Aren't you glad we've separated?

16:49.883 --> 16:54.805
Do their heads need to be cut off
at the same time too?

17:02.438 --> 17:05.024
What is this?

17:06.191 --> 17:07.901
That khakkhara…

17:09.111 --> 17:13.240
Crap. I'm about to lose consciousness.

17:15.451 --> 17:18.662
Someone's on the roof?

17:19.830 --> 17:21.415
Genya?

17:27.504 --> 17:30.841
What is that weapon? Is that a gun?

17:30.924 --> 17:33.177
It smells just like Nichirin Swords.

17:35.220 --> 17:37.139
One of them is still standing.

17:41.852 --> 17:44.730
This is fun. How interesting.

17:44.813 --> 17:47.816
I've never felt an attack
like that before.

17:49.068 --> 17:50.194
Genya! No!

17:50.277 --> 17:52.321
No matter how strong your weapons are,
this demon…

17:54.281 --> 17:55.449
can't be defeated!

17:55.532 --> 17:57.326
They will split every time you kill them!

17:57.409 --> 17:59.828
Then rejuvenate and get stronger!

17:59.912 --> 18:01.997
They're just letting you
cut their heads off!

18:04.541 --> 18:07.377
This demon doesn't care
about having its head cut off.

18:07.753 --> 18:09.630
That means its head's not its weak spot.

18:10.214 --> 18:13.050
Now they have four bodies.
It regenerates so fast.

18:13.133 --> 18:16.428
Isn't there any pattern?
Where does it regenerate fastest?

18:17.012 --> 18:19.431
It must have a weak spot.

18:19.848 --> 18:21.600
Find it! Look for it!

18:22.851 --> 18:24.061
There must be something.

18:25.896 --> 18:28.190
Shouldn't there be four bodies?

18:32.194 --> 18:34.321
What a delightful moment!

18:34.404 --> 18:37.658
It's been a long time since I split up!

18:37.741 --> 18:39.701
This one can fly.

18:39.785 --> 18:41.578
Each of them has different abilities.

18:42.329 --> 18:45.290
Nezuko! Don't worry about me!
Just help Genya--

18:49.128 --> 18:50.003
UPPER - FOUR

18:50.087 --> 18:52.047
You're so weak it's sad.

18:55.425 --> 18:57.803
Genya!

18:57.886 --> 18:59.388
Nezuko, help him!

18:59.471 --> 19:02.266
Help Genya! Please, hurry!

19:03.350 --> 19:06.770
You have the time
to worry about others, huh?

19:10.774 --> 19:12.067
Hinokami Kagura!

19:21.326 --> 19:25.497
He's good. This is quite delightful.

19:25.581 --> 19:26.540
DELIGHT

19:27.708 --> 19:30.002
Grab onto a branch! A branch!

19:41.305 --> 19:44.141
Hurry! Stand up! Get on your feet!

19:44.224 --> 19:47.769
The villagers are in danger.
I have to protect them.

19:47.853 --> 19:50.731
Crap! My body is numb.

19:50.814 --> 19:53.025
I can't hear anything.

20:05.871 --> 20:07.581
I've been blown away quite far.

20:08.123 --> 20:10.167
Must get back as fast as possible.

20:15.172 --> 20:16.673
A demon and a child.

20:17.674 --> 20:22.012
A child must be inexperienced
in swordsmithing skills.

20:22.095 --> 20:24.556
Helping him is low-priority.

20:25.224 --> 20:26.516
From the looks of it,

20:26.600 --> 20:29.978
that's not the main body
but created by some demon arts.

20:34.191 --> 20:36.443
There's no reason to stop here.

20:37.444 --> 20:40.906
If the entire village is under attack,
the number one priority is the chief.

20:40.989 --> 20:44.826
I have to protect those who have
the greatest skills and abilities.

20:48.997 --> 20:51.750
What I need to do now is to eliminate
the Upper Rank demon

20:51.833 --> 20:53.669
and protect the village.

20:55.462 --> 20:58.924
Saving an inexperienced swordsmith won't…

20:59.466 --> 21:03.971
Because helping others eventually
ends up being good for me.

21:20.320 --> 21:21.488
Run.

21:22.739 --> 21:24.074
You…

21:29.413 --> 21:32.541
You'll just get in my way,
so get out of here, will you?

23:06.051 --> 23:07.135
DEMON SLAYER: SWORDSMITH VILLAGE ARC
NO. 3

23:07.886 --> 23:11.389
We're all being attacked by demons
while Haganezuka's polishing your sword.

23:11.473 --> 23:13.600
-Are you okay?
-Yup.

23:13.683 --> 23:17.187
He even made this sword.

23:17.270 --> 23:20.565
But he never changes.

23:20.649 --> 23:23.235
Yeah, his nature will never change.

23:25.028 --> 23:27.405
Now it's time for the Taishō era secret.

23:27.489 --> 23:32.035
Haganezuka attaches wind chimes
to his woven hat because he loves it.

23:32.119 --> 23:34.996
When he was a child,
every time he threw a tantrum,

23:35.080 --> 23:37.332
the adults around him
would ring the wind chimes.

23:37.415 --> 23:38.416
CHIEF TECCHIN'S FACE

23:38.500 --> 23:40.001
You learn something new every day.

23:40.085 --> 23:41.586
This is for you.

23:41.670 --> 23:46.341
If you think that's going to put me
in a good mood, you're wrong!

23:47.092 --> 23:48.552
Ring! Ring! Ring!

23:48.635 --> 23:50.595
Don't treat me like a child!

23:50.679 --> 23:52.013
Ring! Ring! Ring!

23:52.681 --> 23:55.517
Next up on Episode 4: "Thank You, Tokito."

23:55.600 --> 23:56.893
Have you calmed down?

23:56.977 --> 23:58.520
Like I said, don't treat me like a--

23:58.603 --> 23:59.938
Ring! Ring! Ring!

24:00.021 --> 24:00.981
TO BE CONTINUED
